{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via an automated cobbler orchestrator pipeline) requested implementation of srd036-mktemp requirements R3.5, R3.6, R4.1, and R4.2 in the go-unix-utils project. This is task #5350, a \"stitch\" task on branch `task/generation-run44-5350`. The specific requirements are:\n   - **R3.5**: `-u` or `--dry-run` must print the name that would be created without actually creating it, and must print a warning that the option is discouraged.\n   - **R3.6**: `-q` or `--quiet` must suppress error messages on failure.\n   - **R4.1**: Differential tests must compare exit codes and structural properties of output between the Go binary and gmktemp via pkg/testutils.\n   - **R4.2**: Tests must verify structural properties: output is a valid path in the expected directory, the file or directory exists after creation, the name matches the template pattern, and permission bits match the specification.\n\n   Acceptance criteria: AC1 (go build compiles), AC2 (go vet passes), AC3 (all R3.5, R3.6, R4.1, R4.2 behaviors implemented), AC4 (existing functionality not broken). No git commands allowed.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GNU mktemp reimplementation in Go with differential testing against `gmktemp`\n   - Manual CLI flag parsing (no cobra - short flags parsed char by char, long flags with prefix matching)\n   - Dry-run mode (`-u`/`--dry-run`) - print without creating, emit warning\n   - Quiet mode (`-q`/`--quiet`) - suppress stderr error messages\n   - Differential testing via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing structural properties (not exact filenames since random)\n   - SIGPIPE handler convention via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - File permissions: 0600 for files, 0700 for directories\n   - T